From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - check the associated data length of ESP requests

The generic rfc4106, rfc4543 and rfc4309 templates reject a request
whose associated data, which includes the IV, is neither 16 nor 20
bytes long. The driver sends any length to the SPU, and the result
differs from the generic one:

  alg: aead: gmac-aes-esp-iproc encryption unexpectedly succeeded on
  test vector "random: alen=0 plen=128 authsize=16 klen=20 novrfy=0";
  expected_error=-22, ...

Reject it with crypto_ipsec_check_assoclen().

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -2686,6 +2686,9 @@ static int aead_enqueue(struct aead_request *req, bool is_encrypt)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	if (ctx->is_esp && crypto_ipsec_check_assoclen(req->assoclen))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	rctx->gfp = (req->base.flags & CRYPTO_TFM_REQ_MAY_SLEEP) ?
 		       GFP_KERNEL : GFP_ATOMIC;
 	rctx->parent = &req->base;
